WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:48.152 --> 00:50.697
‎1988 GUSEO UNIVERSITY ‎MEDICAL SCHOOL GRADUATION CEREMONY

4
00:52.740 --> 00:54.492
‎Gu Bon-pyeong.

5
01:00.874 --> 01:02.417
‎CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION ‎GU BON-PYEONG

6
01:02.500 --> 01:03.751
‎GUSEO FOUNDATION CHAIRMAN'S AWARD

7
01:03.835 --> 01:06.504
‎Next is Bu Seung-gwon.

8
01:07.088 --> 01:08.173
‎Here!

9
01:10.717 --> 01:13.178
‎DISTINGUISHED SERVICE AWARD ‎BU SEUNG-GWON

10
01:14.554 --> 01:17.182
‎All those awards ‎actually belonged to Bu Seung-gwon,

11
01:17.265 --> 01:19.851
‎but Professor Min agreed ‎to give them to Gu Bon-pyeong

12
01:20.643 --> 01:24.189
‎on the condition that ‎Seung-gwon leads the Hippocratic Oath.

13
01:24.272 --> 01:25.440
‎That's what I heard.

14
01:25.523 --> 01:28.401
‎The chairman's son can have the awards,

15
01:28.484 --> 01:31.529
‎but someone who truly deserves them ‎should lead the oath.

16
01:31.613 --> 01:32.864
‎That's the general idea.

17
01:32.947 --> 01:33.990
‎And he's right.

18
01:34.073 --> 01:35.950
‎Someone who'd actually practice ‎should lead it.

19
01:37.744 --> 01:38.745
‎Good job.

20
01:38.828 --> 01:39.829
‎Thank you.

21
01:40.455 --> 01:41.998
‎HIPPOCRATIC OATH

22
01:47.921 --> 01:52.008
‎Hi… Hippocratic Oath!

23
01:52.091 --> 01:53.760
‎-I pledge! ‎-I pledge!

24
01:53.843 --> 01:58.598
‎"As a member of the medical profession…"

25
01:58.681 --> 02:03.311
‎-As a member of the medical profession… ‎-As a member of the medical profession…

26
02:03.394 --> 02:08.107
‎"I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life ‎to the service of humanity."

27
02:08.191 --> 02:11.945
‎I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life ‎to the service of humanity.

28
02:12.028 --> 02:13.529
‎1996 GUSEO UNIVERSITY

29
02:13.613 --> 02:17.242
‎"I will give to my teachers the respect ‎and gratitude which is their due."

30
02:17.325 --> 02:20.787
‎I will give to my teachers the respect ‎and gratitude which is their due.

31
02:22.413 --> 02:26.376
‎"I will practice my profession ‎with conscience and dignity."

32
02:27.043 --> 02:30.255
‎I will practice my profession ‎with conscience and dignity.

33
02:31.756 --> 02:33.925
‎-One, two, three! ‎-One, two, three!

34
02:36.886 --> 02:38.304
‎-Okay. ‎-One, two, three!

35
02:38.388 --> 02:40.139
‎Hold on. The theater club guys.

36
02:40.223 --> 02:41.057
‎Hey, theater club!

37
02:41.140 --> 02:42.892
‎-Hey, line up. ‎-Guys, get ready.

38
02:42.976 --> 02:44.644
‎Three, two, one!

39
02:44.727 --> 02:46.354
‎-Wilderness! ‎-Wilderness!

40
02:47.063 --> 02:49.357
‎One more! Three, two, one!

41
02:49.440 --> 02:50.608
‎"The health and well-being…"

42
02:50.692 --> 02:54.821
‎"The health and well-being of my patient ‎will be my first consideration."

43
02:56.030 --> 03:00.201
‎"I will respect the secrets ‎that are confided in me."

44
03:01.661 --> 03:02.870
‎"I will maintain

45
03:02.954 --> 03:05.748
‎the honor and noble traditions ‎of the medical profession."

46
03:06.541 --> 03:10.128
‎Diploma issued to Ma Seong-gyu ‎and fellow graduates.

47
03:12.296 --> 03:14.757
‎"My colleagues will be ‎my sisters and brothers."

48
03:14.841 --> 03:15.842
‎Congratulations.

49
03:15.925 --> 03:19.345
‎"I will maintain ‎the utmost respect for human life

50
03:19.429 --> 03:22.015
‎from its very beginning."

51
03:23.474 --> 03:25.018
‎First, let me be clear

52
03:25.101 --> 03:29.272
‎that this decision was not made lightly.

53
03:29.814 --> 03:31.566
‎Negotiations have failed.

54
03:31.649 --> 03:33.401
‎We issue a warning to the government!

55
03:33.985 --> 03:36.612
‎If this measure is not withdrawn,

56
03:36.696 --> 03:38.156
‎all medical associations will mobilize

57
03:38.906 --> 03:41.326
‎to hold an immediate vote ‎on a general strike.

58
03:42.076 --> 03:43.411
‎We also want to make it clear

59
03:44.203 --> 03:48.333
‎that stepping away from our patients ‎is our absolute last resort.

60
03:53.004 --> 03:55.882
‎2026 PRESS CONFERENCE ‎MEDICAL SCHOOL QUOTA INCREASE OPPOSITION

61
03:57.216 --> 03:58.634
‎Hello, I'm Ma Seong-gyu,

62
03:58.718 --> 04:01.346
‎head of the Gyeonggi Chapter ‎of the Korean Intern Resident Association.

63
04:02.138 --> 04:05.475
‎In 42 hours, at 6 a.m. this Wednesday,

64
04:06.059 --> 04:09.562
‎all residents and interns ‎will stop working and leave the hospital.

65
04:10.938 --> 04:14.150
‎"I will not permit considerations ‎of race, religion, nationality,

66
04:14.233 --> 04:16.694
‎political party, social standing,

67
04:17.278 --> 04:19.697
‎or any other factor to intervene

68
04:20.365 --> 04:24.118
‎between my duty and my patient."

69
04:25.787 --> 04:27.580
‎"Even under threat,

70
04:28.289 --> 04:32.085
‎I will not use my medical knowledge ‎contrary to the laws of humanity."

71
04:40.301 --> 04:43.846
‎"I make these promises as a medical doctor

72
04:44.972 --> 04:48.601
‎solemnly, freely, and upon my honor."

73
05:07.537 --> 05:11.040
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

74
05:16.838 --> 05:18.965
‎EPISODE 8

75
05:29.308 --> 05:32.228
‎42 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

76
05:32.979 --> 05:34.564
‎I can't see the margins.

77
05:34.647 --> 05:35.773
‎Placing a retractor.

78
05:35.857 --> 05:37.608
‎-The other side too. ‎-Yes, Dr. Gye.

79
05:37.692 --> 05:38.943
‎Vitals are unstable.

80
05:43.656 --> 05:44.782
‎Oh, come on.

81
05:45.491 --> 05:48.327
‎Teddy bears don't have vitals.

82
05:48.911 --> 05:51.205
‎That damn theater geek.

83
05:51.289 --> 05:52.123
‎You got this!

84
05:52.707 --> 05:55.001
‎"You got this"? What a joke.

85
05:59.589 --> 06:00.464
‎I don't do that.

86
06:02.633 --> 06:04.927
‎How could you flat-out refuse?

87
06:05.011 --> 06:06.304
‎You heartless person!

88
06:06.888 --> 06:09.182
‎Are you saying Dr. Gye, ‎the infamous mad dog of the OR,

89
06:09.265 --> 06:10.850
‎is refusing surgery?

90
06:10.933 --> 06:12.101
‎But this hardly counts as--

91
06:13.019 --> 06:14.478
‎Let's operate for now.

92
06:14.562 --> 06:15.813
‎The guardian is crying.

93
06:15.897 --> 06:17.440
‎Why did you page me again?

94
06:17.523 --> 06:18.649
‎What's this?

95
06:18.733 --> 06:21.944
‎-The stuffing's out. Toss it. ‎-Hey, you'll contaminate it!

96
06:22.528 --> 06:23.779
‎She can hear you from outside.

97
06:23.863 --> 06:24.697
‎I'm leaving.

98
06:24.780 --> 06:26.407
‎-No, wait. ‎-Me too.

99
06:26.490 --> 06:29.327
‎Just open an OR for me. Please?

100
06:29.410 --> 06:30.745
‎Don't be ridiculous. Let go of me.

101
06:30.828 --> 06:31.871
‎Doctor.

102
06:32.371 --> 06:35.249
‎Can you operate on Snuggles?

103
06:35.333 --> 06:39.003
‎Of course, Hyeon-a.

104
06:40.463 --> 06:43.216
‎This is Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

105
06:43.299 --> 06:46.052
‎Wow, it's Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

106
06:47.303 --> 06:48.221
‎Do you know me?

107
06:49.555 --> 06:52.642
‎I heard everyone talking in our ward.

108
06:53.267 --> 06:55.561
‎They say you're the best surgeon.

109
06:56.062 --> 06:59.732
‎Dr. Kim also said you were the best.

110
07:01.817 --> 07:02.944
‎Ward?

111
07:03.611 --> 07:05.863
‎Hyeon-a, you're so smart.

112
07:05.947 --> 07:09.283
‎What made you bring Snuggles ‎to the ER when she got hurt?

113
07:09.367 --> 07:12.578
‎Whenever I collapsed ‎after being discharged,

114
07:12.662 --> 07:14.664
‎they brought me here.

115
07:15.373 --> 07:17.333
‎That's why I brought Snuggles here.

116
07:18.876 --> 07:21.629
‎This is Lee Hyeon-a. ‎She's eight, and she's my friend.

117
07:21.712 --> 07:22.547
‎Right?

118
07:23.130 --> 07:24.966
‎Hyeon-a here is super brave.

119
07:25.049 --> 07:29.554
‎Despite the pain, you always tell us ‎your name and where it hurts, don't you?

120
07:31.556 --> 07:33.849
‎Not even adults can do that.

121
07:33.933 --> 07:34.976
‎You're amazing, Hyeon-a.

122
07:36.185 --> 07:37.395
‎Dr. Gye.

123
07:38.479 --> 07:41.440
‎Will Snuggles live if she gets surgery?

124
07:43.693 --> 07:45.194
‎"Live"?

125
07:46.070 --> 07:47.655
‎I'm not sure

126
07:47.738 --> 07:50.783
‎what you mean by that, but…

127
07:51.534 --> 07:53.244
‎Why don't you just buy a new--

128
07:55.663 --> 07:56.872
‎Seriously?

129
08:08.843 --> 08:10.720
‎Lee Snuggles, six years old.

130
08:10.803 --> 08:12.805
‎The patient has a deep laceration and--

131
08:12.888 --> 08:15.600
‎We control the organ injury first.

132
08:16.225 --> 08:17.310
‎I get it, Doctor.

133
08:17.393 --> 08:19.979
‎I just wanted to try it out, okay?

134
08:22.607 --> 08:24.525
‎That's pretty cool, isn't it?

135
08:26.319 --> 08:29.488
‎I'll get back at him for this.

136
08:30.531 --> 08:32.450
‎Think this will be good enough?

137
08:33.075 --> 08:35.202
‎Vitals are stable now.

138
08:35.286 --> 08:36.495
‎Thank you, Doctor.

139
08:36.996 --> 08:39.415
‎Dr. Gye, you need to take this seriously.

140
08:39.498 --> 08:40.666
‎Hyeon-a's watching.

141
08:44.879 --> 08:47.923
‎Dr. Kim got us a lot of new stuffing.

142
08:48.007 --> 08:49.759
‎Make Snuggles plump and stuff her--

143
08:49.842 --> 08:51.177
‎I'll stuff your mouth.

144
08:51.260 --> 08:52.219
‎Shutting up now.

145
09:07.985 --> 09:08.986
‎This?

146
09:09.737 --> 09:10.780
‎Theluji.

147
09:11.364 --> 09:12.323
‎Snow.

148
09:12.907 --> 09:14.158
‎-"Nun" in Korean. ‎-"Nun."

149
09:14.241 --> 09:15.242
‎Exactly.

150
09:15.910 --> 09:16.911
‎Nun.

151
09:16.994 --> 09:18.871
‎I want to see snow.

152
09:20.081 --> 09:22.500
‎We'll take you to see it ‎before the year ends.

153
09:23.167 --> 09:24.043
‎With Neema.

154
09:28.422 --> 09:29.590
‎This won't do.

155
09:30.633 --> 09:32.009
‎Let me take this off.

156
09:37.139 --> 09:37.973
‎Neema.

157
09:39.433 --> 09:40.267
‎Yes.

158
09:41.060 --> 09:42.353
‎Mkono is "hand."

159
09:42.436 --> 09:43.938
‎-"Hand." ‎-"Son" in Korean.

160
09:44.021 --> 09:46.357
‎-"Son." ‎-Son.

161
09:46.440 --> 09:49.110
‎And this is heart.

162
09:49.193 --> 09:50.695
‎"Simjang" in Korean.

163
09:50.778 --> 09:52.071
‎-‎"Simjang." ‎-"Simjang."

164
09:52.154 --> 09:52.988
‎Simjang.

165
09:53.072 --> 09:54.365
‎-"Simjang." ‎-"Simjang."

166
09:54.448 --> 09:55.408
‎"Sinjang."

167
09:56.534 --> 09:58.202
‎How about this?

168
10:01.288 --> 10:02.540
‎Maeum.

169
10:02.623 --> 10:03.708
‎"Maeum."

170
10:03.791 --> 10:05.501
‎"Maeum."

171
10:05.584 --> 10:07.461
‎Yes. Maeum.

172
10:07.545 --> 10:09.672
‎-"Maeum." ‎-Perfect.

173
10:13.384 --> 10:14.802
‎Dolly!

174
10:43.748 --> 10:46.625
‎LEE SNUGGLES, F/6

175
10:49.003 --> 10:50.004
‎Cut.

176
10:50.087 --> 10:51.046
‎BLOOD PRESSURE CUFF

177
10:51.964 --> 10:53.007
‎I think it's over.

178
11:02.683 --> 11:04.310
‎Hyeon-a, Snuggles is done.

179
11:04.810 --> 11:05.770
‎The surgery went well.

180
11:34.173 --> 11:36.091
‎She has a malignant myofibroblastoma.

181
11:36.675 --> 11:38.260
‎Thank you.

182
11:38.886 --> 11:41.931
‎It's about 15 cm and wrapped around ‎her abdominal organs.

183
11:42.640 --> 11:45.226
‎Palliative chemo is all we can do now.

184
11:45.726 --> 11:48.145
‎Mom, can you wait a minute?

185
11:58.155 --> 11:58.989
‎She already knows

186
11:59.698 --> 12:02.034
‎that no one can operate on her.

187
12:06.288 --> 12:07.248
‎Dr. Gye.

188
12:07.748 --> 12:11.627
‎If I ever leave this world,

189
12:12.253 --> 12:15.589
‎please take care of Snuggles.

190
12:16.799 --> 12:19.343
‎And if she gets sick again,

191
12:19.426 --> 12:21.845
‎please operate on her.

192
12:26.308 --> 12:30.312
‎Promise you won't tell my mom ‎what I just said, okay?

193
12:46.495 --> 12:47.705
‎Hey, Hyeon-a.

194
12:47.788 --> 12:50.791
‎Snuggles got her surgery thanks to me,

195
12:50.874 --> 12:52.876
‎so come visit me again, okay?

196
12:52.960 --> 12:55.921
‎Gummy candies taste the best ‎when I eat them with you.

197
12:57.006 --> 12:58.716
‎These are just for you.

198
12:58.799 --> 12:59.717
‎Okay?

199
13:04.388 --> 13:05.389
‎Good girl.

200
13:11.186 --> 13:12.187
‎Don't run.

201
13:14.607 --> 13:16.650
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL ‎MAKING CHILDREN HAPPY

202
13:20.321 --> 13:21.363
‎She never gave me a hug.

203
13:26.368 --> 13:29.580
‎Dr. Gye, your phone has been buzzing.

204
13:33.375 --> 13:38.339
‎I heard Dr. Gye finally got ‎a desk in the hospital staff room.

205
13:39.590 --> 13:40.424
‎Yes, well…

206
13:41.175 --> 13:43.177
‎There were some circumstances.

207
13:44.011 --> 13:47.014
‎Dr. Gye, how do you like your desk?

208
13:52.728 --> 13:54.438
‎I've never sat there, so…

209
13:54.521 --> 13:57.941
‎I guess you've had ‎a lot of surgeries lately, huh?

210
13:58.525 --> 14:01.737
‎Including Mr. Oh Sang-beom's case,

211
14:01.820 --> 14:04.698
‎Dr. Gye has indeed ‎been a great help to us.

212
14:05.491 --> 14:07.868
‎I'm so happy to hear that.

213
14:07.951 --> 14:10.037
‎I should hand out snacks ‎to her colleagues.

214
14:12.331 --> 14:14.416
‎By the way, this doctor here…

215
14:15.834 --> 14:18.295
‎Aren't you Dr. Jang Gil-yeong ‎of neurosurgery?

216
14:20.506 --> 14:21.548
‎How do you know me?

217
14:21.632 --> 14:23.967
‎You still have your white coat.

218
14:24.510 --> 14:27.262
‎That's right, I still have it. So what?

219
14:27.346 --> 14:29.848
‎You want me to… take it off…

220
14:30.516 --> 14:31.934
‎Are you going to take it off me?

221
14:32.017 --> 14:34.311
‎Dr. Jang, please calm yourself.

222
14:35.270 --> 14:37.147
‎It was a joke.

223
14:37.940 --> 14:39.525
‎Of course, I know who you are.

224
14:39.608 --> 14:42.820
‎You're one of the top neurosurgeons ‎and a master of craniotomy.

225
14:42.903 --> 14:45.489
‎So what? He's never around.

226
14:45.572 --> 14:47.241
‎I told you that wasn't my fault!

227
14:47.324 --> 14:50.828
‎You're rarely around ‎with all those surgeries,

228
14:50.911 --> 14:53.288
‎and I imagine ‎you're busier than ever these days.

229
14:53.789 --> 14:55.958
‎Listen, going forward,

230
14:56.834 --> 14:59.003
‎we'd like you to take on

231
14:59.753 --> 15:01.213
‎our neurosurgery consults.

232
15:01.296 --> 15:02.965
‎Yes, of course.

233
15:03.048 --> 15:06.010
‎If you need more hands on deck, ‎we'll certainly oblige.

234
15:06.093 --> 15:08.262
‎But don't neglect general surgery.

235
15:08.971 --> 15:09.972
‎Of course not.

236
15:10.556 --> 15:12.850
‎I'd say a situation like this

237
15:12.933 --> 15:16.145
‎is when Dr. Gye truly proves her worth.

238
15:16.895 --> 15:19.148
‎Like a jack-of-all-trades, if you will.

239
15:19.857 --> 15:22.735
‎Tell us now if she's board-certified ‎in some other specialty as well.

240
15:22.818 --> 15:24.611
‎Don't spring it on us later.

241
15:24.695 --> 15:26.321
‎Right, so that brings us to…

242
15:27.740 --> 15:29.783
‎this new contract.

243
15:30.284 --> 15:31.618
‎Here you go.

244
15:34.830 --> 15:37.875
‎Given the urgent medical staff shortage,

245
15:37.958 --> 15:42.337
‎we ask you to show ‎a little appreciation for her hard work.

246
15:43.630 --> 15:44.965
‎You want a pay increase.

247
15:45.049 --> 15:47.468
‎Quota increase, pay increase…

248
15:47.551 --> 15:48.719
‎I can't stand it.

249
15:50.220 --> 15:51.472
‎There's a new term.

250
15:55.517 --> 15:58.479
‎"The locum is allowed to perform ‎the surgery she wants."

251
16:02.900 --> 16:04.109
‎You know Wonjae Hospital, right?

252
16:04.193 --> 16:05.360
‎PRIORITIZE DR. GYE'S PREFERENCES

253
16:05.444 --> 16:06.361
‎They called us.

254
16:07.196 --> 16:09.531
‎Apparently, they've heard of Dr. Gye.

255
16:10.574 --> 16:14.953
‎These top-grade melons ‎are extremely hard to get.

256
16:16.080 --> 16:17.790
‎How many should I have ready?

257
16:23.003 --> 16:24.421
‎PATIENTS' RIGHTS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

258
16:24.505 --> 16:26.381
‎WE WILL NOT APOLOGIZE TO PATIENTS

259
16:33.055 --> 16:34.473
‎DOCTORS' STRIKE: OUR FIGHT HAS JUST BEGUN

260
16:39.603 --> 16:40.979
‎Dr. Hwang in neurosurgery is ill.

261
16:41.814 --> 16:44.942
‎The problem is, ‎there's no one to operate on him.

262
16:45.025 --> 16:45.859
‎Who?

263
16:45.943 --> 16:48.195
‎You know, the one who wasn't around, ‎like Dr. Jang.

264
16:48.278 --> 16:50.572
‎The other one whose white coat ‎you threatened to take.

265
16:50.656 --> 16:52.741
‎-Oh, right. ‎-It's not just general surgery.

266
16:52.825 --> 16:55.202
‎Every department is canceling surgeries.

267
16:55.285 --> 16:57.746
‎I can't tell if I'm putting food ‎in my mouth or my nose.

268
16:57.830 --> 16:59.373
‎It's going in your mouth.

269
16:59.456 --> 17:02.835
‎Thanks a lot. Just eat up, ‎so you can do more surgeries.

270
17:04.002 --> 17:05.629
‎Can you stop paging me?

271
17:05.712 --> 17:07.714
‎Why am I the only one ‎you page for surgeries?

272
17:07.798 --> 17:09.883
‎That reminds me, ‎I need you to open an OR--

273
17:09.967 --> 17:10.926
‎Official email requests only.

274
17:11.009 --> 17:14.138
‎I don't remember verbal requests.

275
17:19.309 --> 17:22.020
‎She's overwhelmed ‎because there aren't any doctors.

276
17:22.104 --> 17:23.939
‎I thought anesthesiology would be okay,

277
17:24.439 --> 17:25.274
‎but I guess not.

278
17:25.357 --> 17:28.110
‎You must be busy, young doctor.

279
17:28.193 --> 17:30.028
‎I heard many people walked out.

280
17:31.947 --> 17:32.781
‎Hey…

281
17:42.166 --> 17:44.001
‎I was wondering where they've been.

282
17:46.587 --> 17:48.797
‎You can really feel Dr. Ma's absence.

283
17:49.506 --> 17:51.300
‎All the patients feel uneasy.

284
17:56.972 --> 17:58.765
‎Yes, understood.

285
18:00.309 --> 18:03.812
‎Doctor, I'm afraid we need to ‎cancel the surgery.

286
18:04.313 --> 18:06.481
‎No one can assist you that day.

287
18:08.400 --> 18:10.694
‎That's rather unfair.

288
18:10.777 --> 18:11.737
‎Whose fault do you think--

289
18:12.321 --> 18:13.238
‎Hello?

290
18:13.822 --> 18:14.948
‎Hello?

291
18:16.283 --> 18:17.868
‎There are plenty of ORs.

292
18:17.951 --> 18:21.038
‎But even if Dr. Jo opens one,

293
18:21.121 --> 18:22.247
‎there's no primary surgeon.

294
18:22.331 --> 18:24.041
‎And even if there is one, there's no--

295
18:24.124 --> 18:25.709
‎There's no one to assist.

296
18:25.792 --> 18:28.212
‎And with no one to assist, ‎they can't operate.

297
18:28.295 --> 18:29.963
‎I mean, they won't operate.

298
18:30.047 --> 18:31.048
‎Right.

299
18:31.131 --> 18:33.759
‎But this is when you learn more, Dr. Park.

300
18:34.343 --> 18:36.970
‎You'll get to observe more ‎than those other interns

301
18:37.054 --> 18:38.931
‎and get more chances to scrub in.

302
18:39.723 --> 18:41.934
‎It's not exactly a learning opportunity.

303
18:42.017 --> 18:44.519
‎I'm just so busy tackling ‎whatever work is assigned to me.

304
18:45.229 --> 18:49.149
‎The problem is that ‎they involve people's lives.

305
18:49.233 --> 18:50.234
‎I'm so afraid

306
18:50.817 --> 18:52.110
‎I might miss something.

307
18:52.736 --> 18:55.781
‎They never used to ‎give tasks like that to interns,

308
18:55.864 --> 18:57.616
‎but it's non-stop these days.

309
18:58.116 --> 18:59.117
‎Oh my.

310
18:59.910 --> 19:00.827
‎Excuse us.

311
19:06.458 --> 19:08.543
‎What's the point of a pediatric center?

312
19:09.044 --> 19:11.880
‎The OR situation over there was the same

313
19:11.964 --> 19:14.007
‎even before the recent medical crisis.

314
19:14.091 --> 19:16.260
‎Plenty of ORs, but no surgeons.

315
19:16.843 --> 19:18.262
‎Then why build it?

316
19:18.345 --> 19:21.682
‎Reimbursement rates were low ‎and pediatric surgery was neglected,

317
19:21.765 --> 19:24.184
‎so the government raised the rates ‎a couple of years ago.

318
19:24.268 --> 19:26.270
‎Now there's profit to be made,

319
19:26.353 --> 19:28.897
‎but it's a mess ‎because they rushed everything.

320
19:30.232 --> 19:34.278
‎Hey, the pediatric center will send you ‎lots of consultation requests now.

321
19:35.612 --> 19:36.488
‎I see.

322
19:36.989 --> 19:38.240
‎In that case…

323
19:38.323 --> 19:39.783
‎"I see. In that case"?

324
19:41.618 --> 19:43.245
‎Don't think.

325
19:43.328 --> 19:44.454
‎Don't do anything.

326
19:44.538 --> 19:46.999
‎Just do the surgeries that come in.

327
19:47.082 --> 19:48.667
‎That part about ‎performing surgeries you want?

328
19:48.750 --> 19:51.461
‎I only included it in the contract ‎to raise your morale.

329
19:51.545 --> 19:54.172
‎But what I really wanted ‎was to raise your pay rate.

330
19:54.256 --> 19:56.133
‎I see you thinking.

331
19:56.216 --> 19:58.093
‎You're thinking, ‎and it's making me nervous.

332
19:58.593 --> 20:01.972
‎But I heard pediatric surgery ‎is nothing like adult surgery.

333
20:02.472 --> 20:05.434
‎They say you can crush a vessel ‎just by pressing it.

334
20:05.934 --> 20:07.811
‎So unless you're a pediatric specialist,

335
20:07.894 --> 20:11.064
‎only a few brave, experienced surgeons ‎might consider it,

336
20:11.690 --> 20:13.317
‎since they're so small and fragile.

337
20:15.110 --> 20:19.323
‎Dr. Gye performed ‎a cute and amazing surgery--

338
20:20.782 --> 20:22.576
‎You must be busy. Let's go.

339
20:23.243 --> 20:24.161
‎Be quiet,

340
20:24.244 --> 20:26.580
‎or she'll chew me out for wasting time ‎on something unprofitable.

341
20:27.831 --> 20:29.875
‎The grandmother ‎must've raised those sisters.

342
20:29.958 --> 20:32.878
‎I wonder what her illness is.

343
20:34.463 --> 20:36.131
‎She doesn't look good at all.

344
20:36.214 --> 20:37.174
‎"Doc…"

345
20:37.716 --> 20:40.761
‎"Doctors'…"

346
20:41.511 --> 20:43.263
‎-"Strike." ‎-"Strike."

347
20:44.056 --> 20:45.349
‎"Fi…"

348
20:45.432 --> 20:46.641
‎"Fight."

349
20:47.309 --> 20:49.895
‎Let's go back and read a storybook.

350
20:49.978 --> 20:51.271
‎No.

351
20:54.983 --> 20:59.071
‎"Work stoppage."

352
20:59.988 --> 21:01.323
‎What's that?

353
21:01.406 --> 21:02.324
‎What does it mean?

354
21:03.241 --> 21:04.701
‎Let's go back now.

355
21:04.785 --> 21:07.037
‎Doctors' strike!

356
21:07.120 --> 21:09.998
‎Fight! Work stoppage!

357
21:10.082 --> 21:11.166
‎Be quiet.

358
21:11.249 --> 21:13.126
‎Doctors' strike!

359
21:13.210 --> 21:14.586
‎Work stoppage!

360
21:14.669 --> 21:16.171
‎-I said stop it! ‎-Whatever!

361
21:21.343 --> 21:26.515
‎My little puppy, my little kitten, ‎my little calf.

362
21:27.265 --> 21:30.435
‎My sweet little Ga-eul.

363
21:31.228 --> 21:32.771
‎Me too!

364
21:34.606 --> 21:37.609
‎My sweet little Ga-yeong.

365
21:38.193 --> 21:41.071
‎My little puppy, my little calf…

366
21:41.863 --> 21:45.409
‎my little puppy.

367
21:54.251 --> 21:56.128
‎Yoo Ga-eul, ten years old.

368
21:56.211 --> 21:57.546
‎After a needle biopsy,

369
21:57.629 --> 21:59.506
‎the results came back ‎as ganglioneuroblastoma.

370
22:00.215 --> 22:02.717
‎It's located in the retroperitoneum,

371
22:02.801 --> 22:05.762
‎encasing the aorta, vena cava, ‎right renal artery and vein, and ureter,

372
22:05.846 --> 22:07.639
‎with spinal canal invasion.

373
22:07.722 --> 22:10.392
‎I now see why a consult came in ‎despite the tumor being benign.

374
22:10.475 --> 22:11.726
‎It's quite extensive.

375
22:11.810 --> 22:13.937
‎Yes, clinically it's neuroblastoma.

376
22:14.855 --> 22:16.606
‎She went through eight rounds of chemo,

377
22:16.690 --> 22:18.400
‎but there was no decrease in size.

378
22:19.568 --> 22:21.903
‎Ganglioneuroblastoma…

379
22:21.987 --> 22:23.655
‎It's clear on imaging as well.

380
22:23.738 --> 22:26.741
‎She definitely needs surgery ‎since the tumor in the spinal canal

381
22:26.825 --> 22:28.910
‎is compressing the surrounding structures.

382
22:28.994 --> 22:30.245
‎Surgery was scheduled for tomorrow.

383
22:32.080 --> 22:33.540
‎They're more understaffed than ever,

384
22:33.623 --> 22:36.084
‎so they requested a consult ‎with neuro and general.

385
22:36.668 --> 22:38.712
‎She's probably in a lot of pain.

386
22:39.504 --> 22:41.089
‎Shouldn't we operate right away?

387
22:41.173 --> 22:42.757
‎Of course, we should.

388
22:42.841 --> 22:47.220
‎But they can't work it out right now, ‎so today's agenda is to pass the buck.

389
22:48.555 --> 22:50.640
‎When was the surgery pushed to?

390
22:50.724 --> 22:52.601
‎It's been postponed indefinitely

391
22:53.101 --> 22:55.020
‎because there's no surgeon ‎and no one to assist.

392
22:55.103 --> 22:58.356
‎We looked into transferring her, ‎but everyone is reluctant

393
22:58.440 --> 23:00.901
‎because it's so extensive ‎and requires multiple specialties.

394
23:02.194 --> 23:03.361
‎Director Bu.

395
23:03.445 --> 23:06.072
‎The government ‎is taking legal action against doctors

396
23:06.156 --> 23:09.242
‎who leave their posts ‎to participate in the strike.

397
23:10.994 --> 23:12.120
‎That is…

398
23:13.997 --> 23:15.707
‎Their licenses will be revoked.

399
23:15.790 --> 23:17.667
‎-What? ‎-Have they lost their minds?

400
23:17.751 --> 23:20.921
‎That'll just make more of them walk out, ‎for goodness' sake.

401
23:27.093 --> 23:29.429
‎DR. MA SEONG-GYU

402
23:35.727 --> 23:37.812
‎DR. BAE HEUNG-GON

403
23:43.360 --> 23:44.527
‎He's not answering.

404
23:45.779 --> 23:47.197
‎He's never done this before.

405
23:49.199 --> 23:51.201
‎Feels like he's not picking up on purpose.

406
23:51.284 --> 23:53.245
‎Let's pause the conference for now.

407
23:53.328 --> 23:55.121
‎-Under these circumstances-- ‎-No, we can't.

408
24:02.671 --> 24:03.672
‎I mean…

409
24:04.881 --> 24:06.508
‎then what about this patient?

410
24:07.092 --> 24:09.678
‎MOLLY GOES SHOPPING

411
24:09.761 --> 24:11.721
‎How much longer does she have to hold on?

412
24:13.181 --> 24:15.433
‎38 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

413
24:15.517 --> 24:16.726
‎Please.

414
24:17.894 --> 24:20.230
‎Nurse, I'm begging you.

415
24:21.356 --> 24:22.399
‎I'm sorry.

416
24:22.482 --> 24:23.984
‎I'm so sorry.

417
24:28.613 --> 24:30.991
‎Then what do we do now?

418
24:32.575 --> 24:34.286
‎Where do we go?

419
24:39.040 --> 24:40.333
‎I'm so sorry.

420
24:58.601 --> 25:00.562
‎My little puppy…

421
25:01.438 --> 25:03.315
‎My little kitten…

422
25:04.441 --> 25:06.318
‎My little calf…

423
25:06.901 --> 25:08.695
‎My little chick…

424
25:09.571 --> 25:11.573
‎My little bunny…

425
25:24.627 --> 25:25.628
‎Mom…

426
25:28.506 --> 25:29.507
‎Dad…

427
25:32.344 --> 25:33.470
‎Let me…

428
25:34.804 --> 25:37.098
‎Let me stay just a little longer ‎before I go to you.

429
25:40.226 --> 25:41.644
‎Please help.

430
25:44.189 --> 25:47.984
‎Who'll take care of Grandma and Ga-yeong ‎if I'm not around?

431
25:49.903 --> 25:51.237
‎Help me.

432
25:51.946 --> 25:53.198
‎Please help me.

433
25:59.496 --> 26:02.165
‎Pediatric center, right? What room?

434
26:02.248 --> 26:04.000
‎Dr. Gye, what are you doing?

435
26:04.084 --> 26:06.002
‎Sit back down, Gye.

436
26:07.337 --> 26:08.171
‎Sit.

437
26:09.964 --> 26:10.965
‎Sit!

438
26:11.674 --> 26:14.636
‎He'll need some snacks, at least, ‎to get her to sit.

439
26:15.136 --> 26:16.888
‎Do I need to tranquilize you?

440
26:16.971 --> 26:20.392
‎Explain and leave, or sit down.

441
26:23.144 --> 26:26.356
‎"The locum is allowed to perform ‎the surgery she wants."

442
26:27.148 --> 26:28.149
‎Is this one of those?

443
26:30.276 --> 26:32.404
‎There's no one to assist you.

444
26:32.487 --> 26:34.114
‎An OR and a surgeon alone ‎are not enough to--

445
26:34.197 --> 26:35.740
‎-They're enough. ‎-What?

446
26:35.824 --> 26:37.700
‎I already planned out everything.

447
26:38.368 --> 26:40.703
‎Are you saying ‎you're going to do a solo surgery?

448
26:40.787 --> 26:42.622
‎SOLO SURGERY: PRIMARY SURGEON ‎OPERATING WITHOUT AN ASSISTANT

449
26:45.291 --> 26:46.126
‎It looks like it.

450
26:46.918 --> 26:50.797
‎Look, the hospital can't just stand by ‎and allow such a risky surgery

451
26:50.880 --> 26:53.591
‎to be performed all alone ‎without an assistant.

452
26:53.675 --> 26:56.511
‎You can't bulldoze your way like this ‎even if you're board-certified.

453
26:56.594 --> 26:58.346
‎What happens if things go wrong?

454
26:58.430 --> 26:59.264
‎Then…

455
27:00.432 --> 27:01.474
‎when do we do it?

456
27:03.059 --> 27:05.520
‎We wait until a surgeon's available, ‎then match schedules with others.

457
27:05.603 --> 27:07.188
‎But if there's no OR, then no surgery.

458
27:07.730 --> 27:08.731
‎So tell me when.

459
27:09.357 --> 27:13.153
‎Nobody's clearing their schedule ‎or walking away from the strike to do it.

460
27:13.236 --> 27:15.530
‎-Still, this isn't-- ‎-Have you ever been kicked in the stomach?

461
27:16.406 --> 27:18.408
‎Ever been crushed under a huge rock?

462
27:18.491 --> 27:20.243
‎That 10-year-old is enduring the pain

463
27:21.369 --> 27:22.954
‎of being kicked in the stomach repeatedly.

464
27:23.037 --> 27:26.499
‎It's as if someone placed a huge rock ‎on her stomach.

465
27:27.000 --> 27:27.917
‎If you won't remove it,

466
27:28.501 --> 27:29.586
‎if you won't do anything,

467
27:30.253 --> 27:31.838
‎at least look the other way.

468
27:34.549 --> 27:35.633
‎We're doctors too.

469
27:36.217 --> 27:38.970
‎It's because we're doctors ‎that we can't look the other way!

470
27:39.053 --> 27:40.472
‎If you're a doctor, join me.

471
27:44.851 --> 27:45.852
‎If you're a doctor,

472
27:47.270 --> 27:48.229
‎scrub in with me.

473
28:00.992 --> 28:03.036
‎She's the only doctor ‎with no ties to the strike.

474
28:03.620 --> 28:05.580
‎Use her to fill the gap.

475
28:05.663 --> 28:09.042
‎Online sentiment and public opinion ‎don't look good right now.

476
28:12.629 --> 28:13.671
‎When will you do it?

477
28:14.255 --> 28:17.008
‎Tomorrow at 12 p.m., ‎as originally scheduled.

478
28:17.800 --> 28:18.843
‎What, tomorrow?

479
28:19.552 --> 28:20.762
‎Like, the next day?

480
28:20.845 --> 28:23.181
‎Her pre-ops are done, ‎so we can start on time.

481
28:23.848 --> 28:24.974
‎Right?

482
28:26.809 --> 28:28.311
‎I have another surgery.

483
28:29.145 --> 28:31.439
‎This will take at least ten hours. ‎I can't squeeze it in.

484
28:32.732 --> 28:33.775
‎Six hours tops.

485
28:34.692 --> 28:35.818
‎I'll get it done.

486
28:38.404 --> 28:39.489
‎Dr. Gye.

487
28:43.034 --> 28:46.287
‎If you pull off this surgery in six hours,

488
28:47.413 --> 28:49.332
‎I'll consider ‎a more flexible interpretation…

489
28:51.084 --> 28:52.627
‎of that particular term.

490
28:58.508 --> 29:00.927
‎I don't ever…

491
29:02.470 --> 29:03.513
‎fail.

492
29:07.892 --> 29:09.185
‎I'll pass it on to Ms. Jang.

493
29:25.994 --> 29:28.746
‎I'm going to ask urology ‎to place a double-J.

494
29:28.830 --> 29:30.039
‎I'll call them.

495
29:30.123 --> 29:32.542
‎I'm sorry I can't make it. ‎I have work backed up.

496
29:32.625 --> 29:35.128
‎Having no one is better ‎than having dead weight.

497
29:36.296 --> 29:37.297
‎My feelings aren't hurt.

498
29:37.380 --> 29:38.715
‎What you said is true.

499
29:40.300 --> 29:41.467
‎I'm glad you're operating.

500
29:42.677 --> 29:44.095
‎Can you tell me your plan?

501
29:44.804 --> 29:47.390
‎Open the abdomen, find the tumor, ‎check the major vessels,

502
29:47.473 --> 29:49.434
‎and dissect with minimal trauma.

503
29:49.517 --> 29:51.519
‎The ureter should be fine ‎with the double-J,

504
29:51.603 --> 29:54.814
‎so run a frozen biopsy on tissue ‎around the vessels and ureter.

505
29:54.898 --> 29:57.400
‎-If it's benign tissue, temporarily-- ‎-Temporarily close,

506
29:57.483 --> 29:58.985
‎move on to the spine,

507
30:00.028 --> 30:01.195
‎prep with Ioban,

508
30:01.279 --> 30:04.532
‎flip her to the prone position, ‎proceed with spinal canal mass excision…

509
30:04.616 --> 30:05.575
‎Are you joining?

510
30:06.743 --> 30:07.911
‎I have another surgery.

511
30:08.870 --> 30:10.496
‎If Dr. Gye hadn't stepped up, ‎I would've had to.

512
30:12.290 --> 30:14.292
‎But honestly, ‎I don't feel like I'm up to it.

513
30:14.375 --> 30:17.670
‎I'm worried I might pop ‎those tiny vessels with a mere touch.

514
30:17.754 --> 30:19.631
‎I seriously don't know ‎if this is even possible,

515
30:19.714 --> 30:21.007
‎and I got anxious…

516
30:22.592 --> 30:23.760
‎that I ended up following you out.

517
30:25.511 --> 30:26.346
‎Her parents

518
30:27.138 --> 30:29.057
‎died in a hit-and-run accident.

519
30:29.641 --> 30:32.393
‎-Her grandmother collects waste paper-- ‎-How do you know her so well?

520
30:33.394 --> 30:34.771
‎That hit-and-run

521
30:35.313 --> 30:36.731
‎happened during the 2020 strike.

522
30:36.814 --> 30:39.025
‎They were bounced from ER to ER…

523
30:40.276 --> 30:41.235
‎and made the news.

524
30:42.028 --> 30:44.906
‎The internal bleeding was so severe ‎that by the time they came to me,

525
30:44.989 --> 30:46.240
‎it was too late.

526
30:47.158 --> 30:48.493
‎Only Dr. Kim would take them.

527
30:49.661 --> 30:51.704
‎-Are you the only one who knows? ‎-And Dr. Do.

528
30:52.914 --> 30:54.791
‎That's why we accepted ‎the consultation request.

529
30:54.874 --> 30:56.918
‎We lost her parents to a strike,

530
30:57.001 --> 30:59.754
‎and now we might lose her ‎to another strike?

531
30:59.837 --> 31:01.172
‎Hey, that's pretty harsh.

532
31:01.756 --> 31:04.258
‎We're all doctors here. ‎Don't act like you don't know.

533
31:04.342 --> 31:06.094
‎We didn't lose them to strikes.

534
31:06.177 --> 31:07.345
‎Right.

535
31:08.012 --> 31:09.472
‎You didn't lose them to strikes.

536
31:12.183 --> 31:15.561
‎"I will practice medicine ‎with conscience and dignity."

537
31:17.063 --> 31:19.273
‎You had no conscience or dignity.

538
31:20.274 --> 31:23.152
‎That's why you doctors ‎lost them back then.

539
31:32.704 --> 31:37.125
‎It's painful to watch ‎the media and the public

540
31:37.208 --> 31:40.753
‎write off these collective actions ‎as the arrogance of doctors

541
31:40.837 --> 31:44.132
‎and the selfishness ‎of interns and residents.

542
31:44.966 --> 31:48.177
‎We want to ask ‎who's really forcing doctors

543
31:48.261 --> 31:50.179
‎to leave their patients.

544
31:50.805 --> 31:53.391
‎Right now, at this hospital, ‎50% of the interns and residents

545
31:53.474 --> 31:57.103
‎have already handed in their resignations ‎and stopped working.

546
31:57.186 --> 31:58.604
‎And that pace is picking up.

547
31:58.688 --> 32:02.275
‎How can they put their own interests ‎above people's lives?

548
32:02.358 --> 32:03.443
‎I know.

549
32:03.526 --> 32:07.238
‎Remember the breast cancer patient ‎in the next bed?

550
32:07.321 --> 32:08.573
‎The hospital told her to leave.

551
32:08.656 --> 32:09.866
‎I thought she came for chemo.

552
32:09.949 --> 32:11.617
‎-Exactly. ‎-Oh dear.

553
32:11.701 --> 32:15.747
‎You can't negotiate with doctors ‎through aggressive and unilateral demands.

554
32:23.671 --> 32:24.672
‎Dr. Gye.

555
32:27.383 --> 32:28.342
‎Oh, hello.

556
32:30.553 --> 32:33.806
‎I hear you'll be operating on ‎Ms. Yoo Ga-eul as scheduled.

557
32:35.475 --> 32:37.310
‎You came to tell her that, right?

558
32:40.229 --> 32:42.148
‎Dr. Jo was right.

559
32:42.231 --> 32:44.776
‎She said you'd be lurking ‎near the patient's room.

560
32:45.818 --> 32:47.111
‎Lurking?

561
32:47.195 --> 32:49.655
‎And she said I should help out.

562
32:52.867 --> 32:53.868
‎I'm so glad

563
32:54.452 --> 32:56.746
‎at least one patient ‎can get their surgery on time.

564
32:59.373 --> 33:01.459
‎-Ma'am. ‎-Oh, hello.

565
33:01.542 --> 33:04.170
‎You don't need to worry ‎about Ga-eul's surgery.

566
33:04.879 --> 33:07.381
‎Goodness, thank you so much.

567
33:13.304 --> 33:15.264
‎It's been difficult, hasn't it?

568
33:20.686 --> 33:21.729
‎Hi, Hyeon-a.

569
33:21.813 --> 33:22.980
‎I'm getting my surgery.

570
33:23.773 --> 33:25.358
‎You're so lucky!

571
33:25.441 --> 33:28.027
‎My doctor suddenly disappeared.

572
33:28.111 --> 33:30.988
‎That's not true. They'll come.

573
33:31.072 --> 33:32.532
‎-They'll come. ‎-That's right.

574
33:32.615 --> 33:34.325
‎They'll come. It'll be okay.

575
33:34.408 --> 33:36.577
‎What should we do today?

576
33:37.411 --> 33:39.497
‎-Let's draw pictures. ‎-Okay.

577
33:39.580 --> 33:41.415
‎I drew this myself.

578
33:41.499 --> 33:42.500
‎Wow!

579
33:43.084 --> 33:44.502
‎That's really good.

580
33:44.585 --> 33:47.463
‎Ga-eul is really good at drawing.

581
33:50.383 --> 33:51.467
‎Neema.

582
34:02.395 --> 34:04.021
‎It's her first doll.

583
34:06.399 --> 34:08.317
‎But it could also be her last.

584
34:32.633 --> 34:33.467
‎Here.

585
34:34.468 --> 34:38.556
‎My word, eight rounds of chemo ‎and no decrease in size?

586
34:38.639 --> 34:40.850
‎She must've suffered a lot.

587
34:40.933 --> 34:43.728
‎Good thing Su-jeong's operating ‎before she suffers more.

588
34:43.811 --> 34:46.230
‎I should charge them extra ‎for a solo surgery.

589
34:46.939 --> 34:49.358
‎Leave money out of children's cases.

590
34:49.984 --> 34:50.902
‎All right.

591
34:51.903 --> 34:54.614
‎The nerve posterior ‎to the transverse process

592
34:54.697 --> 34:57.992
‎must be protected as much as possible, ‎since the tumor is mostly benign anyway.

593
34:58.075 --> 35:01.245
‎Preventing nerve damage ‎is critical for this child's future.

594
35:04.332 --> 35:05.750
‎-There's more. ‎-What?

595
35:05.833 --> 35:07.752
‎There's another surgery ‎I want you to look at.

596
35:07.835 --> 35:08.920
‎I can hear you.

597
35:10.880 --> 35:11.756
‎But I won't be doing it.

598
35:19.263 --> 35:21.057
‎Only kids get this, right?

599
35:21.140 --> 35:23.059
‎It mostly occurs in children,

600
35:23.768 --> 35:24.894
‎but it's still rare.

601
35:26.395 --> 35:29.482
‎She held on for a long time. ‎She's a fighter.

602
35:30.399 --> 35:31.400
‎Good girl.

603
35:31.484 --> 35:32.735
‎YOO GA-EUL, F/10

604
35:34.528 --> 35:35.988
‎-Mi-gyeong. ‎-Yes?

605
35:36.739 --> 35:38.491
‎Are you done with internal medicine?

606
35:39.075 --> 35:40.701
‎Are you sticking with general practice?

607
35:48.834 --> 35:51.337
‎I thought I could save my patient.

608
35:53.839 --> 35:55.258
‎I got so angry

609
35:56.425 --> 36:00.054
‎when they said they were in pain ‎and begged me to let them go.

610
36:00.888 --> 36:02.348
‎I couldn't accept it.

611
36:03.641 --> 36:05.726
‎I kept thinking, "Why can't I save them?"

612
36:06.310 --> 36:08.271
‎"Why are they still in pain?"

613
36:08.354 --> 36:10.147
‎Even when I let them go,

614
36:11.148 --> 36:12.566
‎I didn't cry.

615
36:14.443 --> 36:15.903
‎But they smiled and said…

616
36:18.364 --> 36:19.490
‎that it didn't hurt anymore.

617
36:23.327 --> 36:24.370
‎So…

618
36:25.788 --> 36:27.999
‎you save your patients, okay?

619
36:36.048 --> 36:40.094
‎The kids are probably in pain even now.

620
36:40.636 --> 36:41.887
‎Ga-eul.

621
36:42.680 --> 36:44.056
‎Does it hurt a lot?

622
36:45.433 --> 36:47.018
‎Should I call the doctor?

623
36:48.811 --> 36:49.687
‎I'm okay.

624
36:50.271 --> 36:52.940
‎Why are you up, Hyeon-a? ‎Are you having trouble sleeping again?

625
36:53.733 --> 36:54.817
‎I came to give you this.

626
36:55.860 --> 36:58.988
‎You need a shot when you feel sick.

627
36:59.071 --> 37:01.782
‎But you've held back ‎because it costs money.

628
37:02.491 --> 37:03.951
‎I'll give that to you,

629
37:04.035 --> 37:06.329
‎so you can call the doctor today.

630
37:06.829 --> 37:07.788
‎Thanks.

631
37:08.497 --> 37:11.167
‎But I don't need it.

632
37:11.792 --> 37:13.294
‎I'm getting surgery tomorrow.

633
37:14.003 --> 37:15.504
‎I just need to hold on a bit more.

634
37:18.549 --> 37:21.260
‎But your surgery ‎might get postponed again.

635
37:22.261 --> 37:24.847
‎The doctors keep disappearing.

636
37:26.223 --> 37:27.391
‎No.

637
37:27.475 --> 37:31.187
‎The nurse said my doctor won't disappear.

638
37:31.270 --> 37:33.689
‎Really? That's such a relief.

639
37:36.150 --> 37:38.986
‎I hope tomorrow comes soon,

640
37:39.779 --> 37:40.780
‎Mi-gyeong.

641
37:54.710 --> 37:55.711
‎Found it.

642
38:14.313 --> 38:15.147
‎Is this…

643
38:16.190 --> 38:17.274
‎Snuggles?

644
38:21.404 --> 38:22.279
‎Doctor.

645
38:23.239 --> 38:24.240
‎-Doctor! ‎-Dr. Gye.

646
38:25.032 --> 38:26.033
‎-Doctor! ‎-Dr. Gye.

647
38:30.788 --> 38:34.792
‎Come on, energy stick. Get her up.

648
38:41.340 --> 38:44.385
‎I know we had to close the ER ‎due to lack of definitive care,

649
38:44.468 --> 38:46.262
‎but what kind of behavior is this?

650
38:46.345 --> 38:49.306
‎You think the ER is a joke ‎because we had to shut down?

651
38:49.390 --> 38:51.183
‎It's only for a few days.

652
38:51.267 --> 38:52.977
‎The ER is closed?

653
38:53.894 --> 38:55.771
‎Seriously? I had no idea.

654
38:57.398 --> 38:58.399
‎There's a sign out front.

655
38:59.316 --> 39:01.235
‎I suppose you didn't see it.

656
39:01.318 --> 39:02.319
‎NOTICE OF EMERGENCY ROOM CLOSURE

657
39:04.488 --> 39:05.948
‎We couldn't take patients after midnight.

658
39:07.241 --> 39:08.200
‎This is a first for me too.

659
39:08.284 --> 39:10.035
‎We were even open 6 years ago ‎during COVID-19.

660
39:10.703 --> 39:13.038
‎About 70% of the interns ‎and residents walked out.

661
39:14.790 --> 39:16.500
‎This is totally different from back then.

662
39:16.584 --> 39:17.501
‎Send the patients to me.

663
39:17.585 --> 39:19.420
‎Why? Are there ten of you?

664
39:19.503 --> 39:20.588
‎You only need ten?

665
39:21.172 --> 39:23.048
‎Hey, Buzzkill Won-jin, ‎you're as silent as ever.

666
39:23.132 --> 39:24.884
‎Are you here to take her away?

667
39:24.967 --> 39:26.343
‎You seem okay.

668
39:26.927 --> 39:30.181
‎I thought you'd raise hell and scream, ‎"You call yourselves doctors?"

669
39:30.264 --> 39:33.017
‎then find yourself a corner to sob, ‎"I'm sorry."

670
39:34.143 --> 39:35.144
‎Me?

671
39:35.728 --> 39:36.854
‎You're totally wrong.

672
39:36.937 --> 39:38.272
‎No way I'd do that.

673
39:39.023 --> 39:39.982
‎Where are you going?

674
39:42.485 --> 39:45.321
‎You call yourselves doctors?

675
39:46.530 --> 39:47.656
‎I'm sorry.

676
39:48.991 --> 39:50.784
‎I couldn't protect the ER.

677
39:54.079 --> 39:56.165
‎What? I'm totally fine.

678
39:56.248 --> 39:57.791
‎I slept well, so I feel great.

679
40:01.086 --> 40:03.214
‎I bet it's a transfer call!

680
40:03.881 --> 40:05.716
‎Then why are his eyes bloodshot?

681
40:06.258 --> 40:07.510
‎And why are you here?

682
40:07.593 --> 40:08.511
‎Just because.

683
40:09.470 --> 40:11.347
‎I couldn't wait for tomorrow to come,

684
40:11.430 --> 40:13.057
‎so I came early to wait.

685
40:13.140 --> 40:15.309
‎Dr. Kim definitely rubs off on you.

686
40:15.392 --> 40:18.020
‎Now Tae-gyeong and everyone else ‎are just as soppy as he is.

687
40:21.148 --> 40:22.983
‎-We don't have big rooms. ‎-Let's go.

688
40:23.067 --> 40:24.944
‎No, we're not set up like that.

689
40:26.820 --> 40:30.115
‎Hey, you have no right ‎to look so cool just walking away.

690
40:30.199 --> 40:31.742
‎Why do you look cool going into surgery?

691
40:33.410 --> 40:35.538
‎I want to do it too.

692
40:36.247 --> 40:37.122
‎"Suction."

693
40:42.002 --> 40:42.920
‎Dr. Ma.

694
40:43.754 --> 40:44.964
‎What brings you here?

695
40:46.674 --> 40:48.551
‎Are you really packing up?

696
40:48.634 --> 40:50.636
‎-Are you really walking out? ‎-You're staying, right?

697
40:52.096 --> 40:53.430
‎Yes, I'm staying.

698
40:53.973 --> 40:56.141
‎I want you to stay too.

699
40:58.561 --> 40:59.395
‎Get back to work.

700
41:01.689 --> 41:04.900
‎You're getting double board-certified, ‎so there's no time to lose.

701
41:04.984 --> 41:08.237
‎Your patients saw your interview ‎and were really startled--

702
41:08.320 --> 41:09.780
‎What's the point?

703
41:11.031 --> 41:11.865
‎What?

704
41:11.949 --> 41:15.244
‎Why go through hell to become ‎a double board-certified surgeon?

705
41:16.161 --> 41:17.162
‎Like that matters.

706
41:17.955 --> 41:20.541
‎They don't care. They're saying ‎they can just hire more people.

707
41:21.208 --> 41:23.294
‎This is how they treat us

708
41:23.377 --> 41:26.380
‎after all those years of studying ‎and grueling hours of work.

709
41:27.590 --> 41:30.050
‎Instead of giving people a reason to stay,

710
41:30.843 --> 41:32.803
‎they just want to push out ‎more doctors to work.

711
41:32.886 --> 41:35.139
‎What are we, damn machines?

712
41:36.557 --> 41:37.516
‎Dr. Ma.

713
41:41.687 --> 41:43.981
‎Here's the book I borrowed from you.

714
41:44.064 --> 41:46.066
‎-Forget it. Keep it. ‎-No, please.

715
41:46.609 --> 41:47.443
‎Read it again.

716
41:48.277 --> 41:49.361
‎Please.

717
41:50.487 --> 41:51.655
‎What are you doing?

718
41:52.197 --> 41:53.907
‎Get out of his way.

719
42:18.641 --> 42:20.434
‎EMERGENCY RESPONSE COMMITTEE MEETING ‎ON URGENT MATTER

720
42:20.517 --> 42:22.269
‎AGENDA: INTERN AND RESIDENT STRIKE VOTE

721
42:23.228 --> 42:24.313
‎Getting together to vote?

722
42:24.938 --> 42:26.398
‎Shouldn't this be online?

723
42:26.482 --> 42:29.360
‎If it's anonymous, ‎how do we flush out the traitors?

724
42:29.443 --> 42:30.653
‎Miss it, and you're a traitor.

725
42:30.736 --> 42:31.737
‎You call that a vote?

726
42:31.820 --> 42:33.405
‎I knew you wouldn't come.

727
42:33.489 --> 42:36.909
‎Your dad owns a hospital, ‎so you don't care, do you?

728
42:40.704 --> 42:42.915
‎Yeah, I don't care.

729
42:42.998 --> 42:45.292
‎Man, I hate your damn tone.

730
42:45.376 --> 42:48.212
‎-Hey, why did you come here? ‎-What?

731
42:48.295 --> 42:50.339
‎You graduated from Yeongsin University.

732
42:51.173 --> 42:53.634
‎Let's be real. ‎Your school is way more prestigious

733
42:53.717 --> 42:55.177
‎than a random school like Guseo.

734
42:56.387 --> 42:57.763
‎And you're in a branch hospital too.

735
42:57.846 --> 42:59.473
‎Excessively self-aware, aren't you?

736
42:59.973 --> 43:01.350
‎Hey, Park Tae-gyeong.

737
43:01.433 --> 43:03.102
‎You didn't get into trouble there.

738
43:03.185 --> 43:05.896
‎So why'd you leave that place ‎to come here?

739
43:06.438 --> 43:08.607
‎-Did you run a background check? ‎-It's a small field.

740
43:08.691 --> 43:10.234
‎So it's easy to ask around.

741
43:10.984 --> 43:13.237
‎Out of 140,000 doctors in Korea,

742
43:13.320 --> 43:15.698
‎a little over 8,000 of them ‎are interns and residents.

743
43:15.781 --> 43:19.451
‎Those 8,000 are the ones ‎running every university hospital.

744
43:19.535 --> 43:23.080
‎But after breaking our backs for them, ‎we got stabbed in the back.

745
43:23.831 --> 43:27.000
‎And out of those 8,000, ‎you're the biggest sellout.

746
43:27.584 --> 43:29.795
‎Why'd you come here to screw us over?

747
43:29.878 --> 43:31.130
‎You're dragging our numbers down.

748
43:31.213 --> 43:34.758
‎It's because this selfish asshole has ‎a hospital-director daddy to fall back on.

749
43:39.054 --> 43:39.888
‎Hey.

750
43:40.889 --> 43:42.891
‎That pretty much applies ‎to everyone here, no?

751
43:45.102 --> 43:48.063
‎I mean, is anyone here not a doctor's son?

752
43:49.189 --> 43:50.399
‎Your dad's an ophthalmologist.

753
43:51.108 --> 43:52.484
‎Your mom's a dermatologist.

754
43:52.568 --> 43:53.527
‎And yours is…

755
43:54.611 --> 43:56.029
‎a veterinarian, right?

756
43:56.113 --> 43:58.282
‎-Which is why you're so insecure. ‎-You bastard.

757
43:58.365 --> 44:00.784
‎So is anyone here not a doctor's son?

758
44:01.744 --> 44:02.911
‎Hey.

759
44:02.995 --> 44:04.580
‎Who became a doctor ‎because they were poor?

760
44:05.956 --> 44:08.250
‎Who became a doctor to save lives?

761
44:08.834 --> 44:11.712
‎You bastards became doctors ‎because you had money.

762
44:11.795 --> 44:14.339
‎And you became doctors ‎to make even more money.

763
44:14.423 --> 44:17.468
‎Now you're on a goddamn strike ‎while using patients' lives as collateral.

764
44:18.135 --> 44:22.097
‎How can you call your colleagues traitors ‎for choosing to stay and treat patients?

765
44:23.056 --> 44:23.891
‎Hey.

766
44:25.142 --> 44:25.976
‎Hey.

767
44:26.810 --> 44:28.020
‎Listen.

768
44:28.771 --> 44:31.940
‎You're the selfish assholes ‎with zero conscience.

769
44:32.024 --> 44:35.027
‎-You're an errand boy for a random temp! ‎-What did you say?

770
44:35.110 --> 44:36.862
‎What the hell are you doing?

771
44:37.946 --> 44:38.781
‎Park Tae-gyeong.

772
44:42.326 --> 44:43.327
‎Want to get disciplined?

773
44:44.745 --> 44:46.163
‎Do I need to call Dr. Gye?

774
45:01.553 --> 45:02.554
‎Let him go.

775
45:03.263 --> 45:04.097
‎If you don't,

776
45:04.181 --> 45:07.100
‎I'll make sure you end up ‎seeing Dr. Kim as a patient.

777
45:15.651 --> 45:17.444
‎Now's your chance. Hit him, Tae-gyeong!

778
45:17.528 --> 45:18.695
‎Are you serious?

779
45:19.530 --> 45:20.364
‎You three, leave.

780
45:24.701 --> 45:25.536
‎You forgot something.

781
45:26.537 --> 45:27.454
‎You need to apologize

782
45:27.538 --> 45:31.375
‎to the random temp and her errand boy.

783
45:39.258 --> 45:41.093
‎Why didn't you stop them if you were here?

784
45:41.176 --> 45:44.972
‎Why didn't you come in earlier ‎if you were at the door?

785
45:47.683 --> 45:50.060
‎I was listening in ‎because it got interesting.

786
45:50.769 --> 45:52.896
‎Tae-gyeong here sounded ‎totally out of character.

787
45:54.189 --> 45:55.065
‎I'm sorry.

788
45:55.148 --> 45:56.191
‎What for?

789
45:56.733 --> 45:58.360
‎If I hadn't said anything…

790
45:58.443 --> 45:59.778
‎You graduated from Yeongsin, huh?

791
46:01.196 --> 46:04.157
‎That's why you have no friends ‎among the interns and residents,

792
46:04.241 --> 46:06.034
‎who are mostly Guseo graduates.

793
46:07.578 --> 46:08.537
‎I'm sorry.

794
46:10.080 --> 46:11.373
‎What for?

795
46:17.170 --> 46:18.505
‎Why did you come here?

796
46:19.047 --> 46:21.133
‎You know how Guseo graduates can be.

797
46:21.216 --> 46:22.217
‎Well…

798
46:22.301 --> 46:25.137
‎I just wanted to study ‎at a different school.

799
46:25.721 --> 46:27.222
‎Yeah? That's it?

800
46:28.223 --> 46:29.808
‎Is that so?

801
46:29.891 --> 46:32.185
‎-I thought you had surgery this morning-- ‎-It's over.

802
46:34.479 --> 46:37.399
‎Man, I really wanted to take a nap ‎before the next one.

803
46:37.482 --> 46:38.358
‎It's time to go.

804
46:54.541 --> 46:56.293
‎MOM

805
47:03.342 --> 47:06.053
‎Ms. Yoo Ga-eul's surgery ‎is scheduled for 12 p.m., right?

806
47:12.225 --> 47:14.227
‎You thought her sister's name ‎was Gyeo-eul, right?

807
47:15.187 --> 47:16.563
‎It's Ga-yeong.

808
47:18.231 --> 47:20.150
‎Despite her name, ‎Ga-eul wasn't born in autumn.

809
47:20.942 --> 47:22.903
‎Her grandmother never had it easy,

810
47:23.487 --> 47:25.989
‎so she gave her that name, ‎hoping she'd have a bountiful life.

811
47:26.948 --> 47:29.743
‎Her mother held on for a few days ‎before passing.

812
47:32.245 --> 47:34.456
‎Her grandmother came ‎with Ga-yeong on her back,

813
47:34.539 --> 47:35.707
‎holding Ga-eul's hand.

814
47:43.382 --> 47:45.008
‎Are you sure you can do this solo?

815
47:45.842 --> 47:47.177
‎I was wrong.

816
47:47.886 --> 47:49.846
‎It's better to have ‎no conscience and no dignity

817
47:49.930 --> 47:51.473
‎than to have a little of either.

818
47:53.308 --> 47:55.477
‎I'm saying you can't afford to fail.

819
47:55.560 --> 47:57.479
‎Do you know any doctor who can?

820
48:01.108 --> 48:02.192
‎Look here, Gye Su-jeong!

821
48:06.363 --> 48:10.200
‎Dr. Bae, Director Bu, and I ‎have all failed before.

822
48:10.826 --> 48:12.953
‎That goes for all doctors.

823
48:13.787 --> 48:16.915
‎Some of us fall apart afterward ‎and start hoping for something in return.

824
48:17.457 --> 48:20.043
‎So we go on strike, ‎and some of us even leave the field!

825
48:21.628 --> 48:23.547
‎The fear of failure is overwhelming…

826
48:25.298 --> 48:26.591
‎and its results are devastating.

827
48:27.968 --> 48:31.555
‎So how can you talk about failure ‎so casually?

828
48:31.638 --> 48:34.141
‎How can you claim you won't fail?

829
48:35.100 --> 48:36.435
‎You're a doctor too!

830
48:43.108 --> 48:44.025
‎Dr. Do Yun-sik.

831
48:46.403 --> 48:49.573
‎Do you know what sets us apart?

832
48:51.825 --> 48:55.787
‎I scrub in myself ‎because I don't want to fail.

833
48:55.871 --> 48:56.747
‎But you…

834
48:57.581 --> 49:00.792
‎You don't because you don't want to fail.

835
49:05.297 --> 49:06.298
‎We…

836
49:07.090 --> 49:08.425
‎We'll have to close up.

837
49:08.508 --> 49:09.426
‎Dr. Do.

838
49:09.926 --> 49:11.803
‎Are you really going to close up?

839
49:13.138 --> 49:14.681
‎Don't you think

840
49:14.765 --> 49:17.976
‎you should do everything you can now ‎so you can tell him that later?

841
49:18.977 --> 49:20.228
‎I don't fail

842
49:21.313 --> 49:24.357
‎because I can't afford to fail.

843
49:37.871 --> 49:39.372
‎The camera is in place.

844
49:40.207 --> 49:41.249
‎Let's begin.

845
49:52.636 --> 49:53.720
‎Harmonic.

846
50:07.609 --> 50:08.777
‎I don't fail

847
50:09.402 --> 50:12.113
‎because I can't afford to fail.

848
50:18.537 --> 50:19.788
‎Let's start the time-out.

849
50:24.918 --> 50:26.378
‎Let's begin.

850
50:28.463 --> 50:30.090
‎Let's do a time-out.

851
50:31.091 --> 50:32.634
‎What's the patient ID number?

852
50:35.262 --> 50:38.598
‎It's 2-0-2-6… 0-7-0…

853
50:39.516 --> 50:41.351
‎Dr. Hwang! Are you okay?

854
50:41.852 --> 50:43.353
‎Please page someone! Hurry!

855
50:44.020 --> 50:47.440
‎Effective immediately, ‎the government is ordering

856
50:47.524 --> 50:49.693
‎all interns and residents to stay on duty.

857
50:50.360 --> 50:53.113
‎We reiterate that failure to comply

858
50:53.196 --> 50:57.033
‎will result in license revocation ‎and legal penalties.

859
50:57.117 --> 51:00.036
‎A separate return-to-work order ‎will be issued

860
51:00.120 --> 51:02.831
‎pursuant to Article 59 ‎of the Medical Service Act…

861
51:05.041 --> 51:06.084
‎Hey, Hwang!

862
51:06.167 --> 51:07.627
‎Wake up!

863
51:07.711 --> 51:08.628
‎Hwang!

864
51:10.046 --> 51:11.715
‎What is it? Who's the patient?

865
51:12.340 --> 51:13.800
‎What's the surgery? Put up the CT scans.

866
51:13.884 --> 51:15.343
‎How far did he get?

867
51:15.427 --> 51:19.097
‎Doctors who collectively ‎and without justifiable cause…

868
51:19.180 --> 51:21.141
‎They've lost their minds.

869
51:21.224 --> 51:23.977
‎Are they threatening to arrest us doctors?

870
51:25.270 --> 51:27.564
‎Doctors or medical facility founders…

871
51:27.647 --> 51:30.609
‎Dr. Ma, you saw the news, right? ‎Come to the director's office.

872
51:31.484 --> 51:33.236
‎A return-to-work order?

873
51:33.320 --> 51:35.864
‎How is this different from forced labor?

874
51:36.865 --> 51:38.700
‎This will just make things worse.

875
51:39.659 --> 51:41.703
‎Med school students are pushing back too.

876
51:41.786 --> 51:44.956
‎Of course, they are. ‎Kids these days hate stuff like that.

877
51:45.498 --> 51:47.667
‎It's actually better this way.

878
51:47.751 --> 51:50.587
‎People will get a reality check ‎once they suffer without doctors.

879
51:50.670 --> 51:54.007
‎If patients are affected ‎due to the doctors' strike,

880
51:54.090 --> 51:57.594
‎it won't serve as grounds ‎for exemption from liability.

881
51:57.677 --> 51:59.930
‎Seriously, what's the matter with you?

882
52:00.013 --> 52:01.848
‎That reality check you mentioned

883
52:02.474 --> 52:05.352
‎could lead to lawsuits.

884
52:05.435 --> 52:06.978
‎Director Bu!

885
52:07.062 --> 52:08.897
‎Stop raining on our parade!

886
52:08.980 --> 52:10.398
‎We already lived through this

887
52:10.482 --> 52:13.151
‎during the 2000 medical separation strike.

888
52:13.234 --> 52:16.112
‎An unconscious four-year-old ‎was taken to the hospital

889
52:16.196 --> 52:17.781
‎but couldn't get surgery ‎due to the strike,

890
52:17.864 --> 52:20.200
‎and their condition worsened dramatically.

891
52:20.283 --> 52:21.660
‎The family sued,

892
52:21.743 --> 52:25.121
‎and the hospital was ordered to pay ‎300 million won in damages.

893
52:25.872 --> 52:27.165
‎As doctors,

894
52:27.832 --> 52:29.334
‎I'm sure you two will remember.

895
52:44.432 --> 52:46.601
‎It's been a while, Dr. Ma.

896
52:49.938 --> 52:52.148
‎How's the preparation going?

897
52:55.151 --> 52:56.152
‎I'm doing my best, sir.

898
52:58.029 --> 52:59.781
‎-Dr. Ma-- ‎-Director.

899
53:00.949 --> 53:04.035
‎Dr. Hwang Min-gu of neurosurgery ‎collapsed in the OR.

900
53:09.332 --> 53:11.668
‎-Good work, Doctor. ‎-Good job.

901
53:11.751 --> 53:12.752
‎Thank you all.

902
53:20.552 --> 53:23.972
‎Dr. Hwang's surgery was in two days, ‎but it was postponed.

903
53:24.055 --> 53:25.765
‎He was feeling okay,

904
53:25.849 --> 53:28.727
‎so he insisted on ‎doing his surgeries without delay.

905
53:28.810 --> 53:30.520
‎He said once he became a patient himself,

906
53:30.603 --> 53:32.981
‎he understood what it's like ‎to have surgery pushed back.

907
53:33.064 --> 53:34.399
‎That's not like him at all.

908
53:34.482 --> 53:36.359
‎That's not true.

909
53:36.443 --> 53:39.487
‎He's very dedicated ‎when it comes to his cases.

910
53:39.571 --> 53:42.407
‎The problem is that he's a patient too.

911
53:52.292 --> 53:54.669
‎Dr. Kim. Dr. Hwang was here, right?

912
53:54.753 --> 53:56.880
‎Yes, they just took him up to the OR.

913
53:56.963 --> 53:58.840
‎What? Who's operating?

914
53:58.923 --> 54:01.259
‎There aren't any general surgeons.

915
54:02.343 --> 54:03.386
‎Oh, Dr. Bae?

916
54:04.345 --> 54:05.430
‎Dr. Kim.

917
54:05.930 --> 54:07.182
‎How's Dr. Hwang?

918
54:21.529 --> 54:24.074
‎A solo laparoscopic procedure?

919
54:24.866 --> 54:26.326
‎This is insane.

920
54:27.118 --> 54:30.997
‎A solo laparoscopic caudate lobectomy

921
54:31.081 --> 54:34.292
‎is something I've only seen done once ‎at Johns Hopkins.

922
54:34.375 --> 54:35.251
‎Only a very few…

923
54:36.294 --> 54:39.047
‎could pull that off in Korea.

924
54:39.130 --> 54:40.632
‎Dr. Gye is proving…

925
54:42.175 --> 54:43.802
‎that she's one of the few.

926
54:48.181 --> 54:51.684
‎Dr. Gye, what about ‎Ms. Yoo Ga-eul's surgery at 12 p.m.?

927
54:51.768 --> 54:52.769
‎At 12 p.m.?

928
54:53.728 --> 54:55.396
‎It's already past 11 a.m.

929
54:55.480 --> 54:56.981
‎That's why she went in laparoscopically.

930
54:57.565 --> 54:59.317
‎She says she can make it there by 12 p.m.

931
55:03.446 --> 55:05.365
‎-You could push back-- ‎-No.

932
55:05.865 --> 55:07.200
‎I'll make it no matter what.

933
55:08.118 --> 55:10.495
‎I won't let her suffer ‎for even a minute longer.

934
55:17.627 --> 55:18.711
‎Come on.

935
55:19.879 --> 55:21.798
‎Just a bit faster.

936
55:23.258 --> 55:24.425
‎Faster…

937
55:38.857 --> 55:40.316
‎I think she'll make it.

938
55:41.401 --> 55:42.360
‎Right?

939
55:44.070 --> 55:44.904
‎That's a relief.

940
55:47.407 --> 55:49.159
‎I have a surgery to get to, sir.

941
55:49.242 --> 55:51.077
‎Me too, sir.

942
56:05.925 --> 56:06.759
‎Dr. Bae.

943
56:07.927 --> 56:08.803
‎Yes?

944
56:10.096 --> 56:11.097
‎Do you think…

945
56:13.516 --> 56:15.101
‎we failed?

946
56:18.563 --> 56:19.731
‎What do you mean?

947
56:20.440 --> 56:23.902
‎She really has her work cut out for her ‎in that huge OR.

948
56:23.985 --> 56:26.988
‎But there's no one to assist, ‎so she has only herself to rely on.

949
56:28.156 --> 56:30.491
‎Yet she's holding the laparoscope ‎to save a life.

950
56:30.575 --> 56:31.576
‎You know,

951
56:32.160 --> 56:33.786
‎that surgery-obsessed mad dog.

952
56:36.039 --> 56:37.290
‎For the first time,

953
56:38.082 --> 56:39.751
‎I see her ‎not as a surgery-obsessed mad dog,

954
56:40.668 --> 56:43.087
‎but as Gye Su-jeong, ‎a doctor obsessed with saving lives.

955
56:48.134 --> 56:49.052
‎Did we lose?

956
56:51.888 --> 56:54.807
‎The strike seems pretty trivial now.

957
56:59.270 --> 57:00.855
‎I think she'll wrap up pretty soon.

958
57:01.522 --> 57:02.565
‎She might

959
57:03.316 --> 57:06.152
‎even get to grab a sandwich ‎before her next surgery.

960
57:11.241 --> 57:12.450
‎Seong-gyu…

961
57:14.619 --> 57:15.870
‎didn't show up.

962
57:15.954 --> 57:18.665
‎He's with President Kim and Mayor Im--

963
57:18.748 --> 57:20.124
‎I support the strike.

964
57:20.625 --> 57:22.418
‎I'm behind it, but…

965
57:23.962 --> 57:26.297
‎Seong-gyu should be observing that.

966
57:27.382 --> 57:29.217
‎He needs to observe it

967
57:29.759 --> 57:31.344
‎because observing procedures like that

968
57:31.928 --> 57:34.472
‎will help him immensely.

969
57:36.349 --> 57:39.394
‎It feels like he's missing out ‎on every important moment.

970
57:43.648 --> 57:46.484
‎25 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

971
57:46.568 --> 57:48.945
‎2026 INTERN AND RESIDENT ‎EMERGENCY RESPONSE COMMITTEE MEETING

972
57:50.321 --> 57:52.073
‎We'll begin as soon as ‎the reporters arrive.

973
57:52.156 --> 57:54.325
‎You'd better do a good job. ‎I'll be watching you.

974
57:54.409 --> 57:57.161
‎-That's enough. Get up there. ‎-Yes, of course.

975
58:04.419 --> 58:08.423
‎If you see your mom and dad ‎while you're asleep,

976
58:08.506 --> 58:10.049
‎don't follow them.

977
58:10.633 --> 58:11.551
‎Okay?

978
58:14.053 --> 58:16.764
‎I still hope I get to see them.

979
58:18.391 --> 58:21.060
‎Ga-eul, if you see Mom and Dad,

980
58:21.144 --> 58:23.354
‎tell them to visit me in my dreams.

981
58:23.438 --> 58:25.523
‎I don't remember them well,

982
58:25.607 --> 58:28.943
‎so they have to let me know ‎they're Mom and Dad.

983
58:29.027 --> 58:31.738
‎Make sure you tell them that, okay?

984
58:32.655 --> 58:33.906
‎Okay, I will.

985
58:49.297 --> 58:50.965
‎Twenty-two minutes left.

986
59:01.434 --> 59:02.894
‎Just a bit more…

987
59:27.710 --> 59:29.087
‎Wait.

988
59:29.170 --> 59:30.546
‎Good…

989
59:31.422 --> 59:33.049
‎Good job, Doctor.

990
59:45.728 --> 59:47.021
‎ENERGY DRINK

991
59:51.359 --> 59:55.363
‎All university hospitals have this statue.

992
59:55.446 --> 59:58.116
‎Incoming students ‎take photos in front of it.

993
59:58.199 --> 01:00:00.827
‎The statue here is quite large.

994
01:00:04.664 --> 01:00:08.459
‎They say she's Doctor X.

995
01:00:10.586 --> 01:00:13.339
‎-Excuse me? ‎-Dr. Bae and Dr. Ma found an article

996
01:00:13.423 --> 01:00:17.301
‎while looking for reference materials ‎on Mr. Park Gwang-cheol's surgery.

997
01:00:18.970 --> 01:00:22.432
‎It said a certain Doctor X ‎performed the same procedure.

998
01:00:24.559 --> 01:00:25.518
‎Is that so?

999
01:00:26.561 --> 01:00:29.689
‎Well, it's a big world ‎with all sorts of surgical procedures

1000
01:00:29.772 --> 01:00:31.816
‎and doctors to match.

1001
01:00:32.692 --> 01:00:34.110
‎I didn't believe it.

1002
01:00:34.694 --> 01:00:37.864
‎Of course not. ‎Why would you believe such a rumor?

1003
01:00:37.947 --> 01:00:39.240
‎However,

1004
01:00:39.323 --> 01:00:40.992
‎after watching today's surgery,

1005
01:00:41.075 --> 01:00:43.453
‎it made me realize it could be true.

1006
01:00:45.830 --> 01:00:47.373
‎What do you mean?

1007
01:00:50.251 --> 01:00:53.796
‎Dr. Gye and Dr. Ma are the same age.

1008
01:00:53.880 --> 01:00:56.924
‎To be that surgically talented at her age

1009
01:00:57.008 --> 01:00:59.635
‎and to be willing to give it her all--

1010
01:00:59.719 --> 01:01:00.845
‎Director Bu.

1011
01:01:00.928 --> 01:01:02.472
‎Dr. Gye is indeed

1012
01:01:03.097 --> 01:01:04.724
‎an exceptional genius.

1013
01:01:04.807 --> 01:01:07.226
‎But she also worked incredibly hard.

1014
01:01:07.810 --> 01:01:10.605
‎It's upsetting to hear you ‎cast doubt on her like that.

1015
01:01:13.524 --> 01:01:16.569
‎At a time when this statue ‎of Hippocrates and his oath

1016
01:01:17.320 --> 01:01:18.946
‎are being used as a mere photo backdrop

1017
01:01:19.030 --> 01:01:22.950
‎or as a background prop ‎to the ongoing strike,

1018
01:01:23.493 --> 01:01:26.537
‎I can't help but wonder ‎who Gye Su-jeong really is.

1019
01:01:32.960 --> 01:01:34.086
‎I think I've heard enough.

1020
01:01:35.046 --> 01:01:36.964
‎Excuse me. It's almost time for surgery.

1021
01:01:37.548 --> 01:01:38.758
‎Is Gye Su-jeong…

1022
01:01:40.426 --> 01:01:41.719
‎Is Gye Su-jeong…

1023
01:01:58.444 --> 01:02:00.363
‎Let's begin the surgery.

1024
01:02:06.285 --> 01:02:07.954
‎OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

1025
01:02:08.996 --> 01:02:10.581
‎Is Gye Su-jeong…

1026
01:02:13.501 --> 01:02:16.337
‎Doctor X?

1027
01:03:00.256 --> 01:03:03.217
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1028
01:03:42.340 --> 01:03:45.301
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1029
01:03:45.384 --> 01:03:48.137
‎We need to walk away from this hospital.

1030
01:03:48.220 --> 01:03:49.597
‎I need to do this surgery.

1031
01:03:49.680 --> 01:03:53.017
‎No, it'll make you ‎look more like Doctor X.

1032
01:03:53.100 --> 01:03:54.894
‎There's literally no surgical procedure.

1033
01:03:54.977 --> 01:03:56.979
‎That child has no time.

1034
01:03:57.063 --> 01:03:58.648
‎Are you putting ‎a patient's life on the line

1035
01:03:58.731 --> 01:04:01.192
‎to risk other people's careers?

1036
01:04:01.275 --> 01:04:04.070
‎I'm trying to save the life ‎of an eight-year-old patient.

1037
01:04:04.654 --> 01:04:06.072
‎If you do that surgery,

1038
01:04:06.155 --> 01:04:07.573
‎I'm really going to fire you.

1039
01:04:07.657 --> 01:04:09.992
‎Do you think anyone will take part?

1040
01:04:10.076 --> 01:04:10.993
‎Please.

1041
01:04:12.203 --> 01:04:16.874
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
